==English==
{{was wotd|2011|June|23}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|phōca||seal}} (from {{der|en|grc|φώκη}}) {{suffix|en||ine}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈfəʊsʌɪn/|/ˈfəʊsiːn/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-phocine.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Pertaining to a [[seal]] (or similar [[pinniped]]s); [[seallike]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|28 December 1871|||New York Daily Standard|text=He telegraphed to the whaling ports of New England, and sent messages to San Francisco and Alaska, to know if a group of sea lions and other specimens of the '''phocine''' tribe could be secured.}}
#* {{RQ:Nabokov Lolita|text=she had already yanked out of me the coveted section [of the newspaper] and retreated to her mat near her '''phocine''' mamma.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|1987|{{w|William Boyd (writer)|William Boyd}}|The New Confessions|text=She walked over towards me with an odd elegance, big strides, like a champion girl swimmer, say; muscled but lean, with a '''phocine''' grace.}}

